   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "twenty-one separate focalizants in Tigana, and more than 150 separate focalizations"
  },
  {
   "feature": "delayed counter-focalizant",
   "claim": "Kleander shows Part One's twenty-two focalizations (twelve through Devin) uphold a simple good/evil quest before Part Two hands nine of twelve sections to Dianora and demolishes the image of Brandin as evil.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "made up of twenty-two separate focalizations"
  },
  {
   "feature": "antagonist focalized once, late",
   "claim": "Kleander notes Brandin, who originates the whole fabula, is focalized through only once, for about a page at the end of the battle, after the reader has already formed a judgment.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "No more than a page long, Brandin’s focalization"
  },
  {
   "feature": "prologue as mosaic of focalizations",
   "claim": "Kleander quotes Kay that the prologue of Sailing to Sarantium was written as a mosaic of different focalizations.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "the prologue of Sailing to Sarantium was written as a mosaic"
  },
  {
   "feature": "telescoping of events",
   "claim": "Kleander documents Kay's admitted 'telescoping' (iconoclasm moved centuries earlier; a 750-year Reconquista compressed to one lifetime) so that historical loss lands on the same set of characters and intensifies emotional response.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "intensify the emotional and intellectual response to what really happened"
  },
  {
   "feature": "accumulation of detail",
   "claim": "Kleander quotes Kay's stated method of a quiet, steady accumulation of detail and complexity that reaches readers subliminally and builds trust.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "quiet, steady accumulation of detail and complexity"
  },
  {
   "feature": "retrospective hints",
   "claim": "Kleander observes that Kay plants hints to Valentin's identity as Rhun throughout Tigana which only make sense in retrospect.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "the hints only make sense in retrospect"
  },
  {
   "feature": "withheld duel outcome",
   "claim": "Kleander notes that who survived the Ammar–Rodrigo duel is not revealed until halfway through the epilogue, by which point the outcome is 'strangely unimportant'.",
   "source": "Anya Kleander, 'Present Reality in Historical Fantasy' (Honours dissertation, University of Stirling, 2008)",
   "url": "https://brightweavings.com/presentreality/",
   "quote": "not until halfway through the epilogue that Kay reveals who survived"
  },
  {
   "feature": "parallel-structured prayer passages",
